<title>PHILIPPINES: Empire sets dividend, capital increase.</title>
<headline>Empire sets dividend, capital increase.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mass-housing builder Empire East Land Holdings Inc said on Thursday its board had approved an 88 percent stock dividend.</p>
<p>Empire East also said in a statement to the Philippine Stock Exchange that its board approved an increase in the firm's authorised capital from three billion pesos to eight billion.  </p>
<p>A year-ago comparison on the stock payout was not available as the company went public last June.</p>
<p>The firm said the stock dividend declaration and the proposed capital increase will have to be approved by shareholders in its annual meeting on April 25.</p>
<p>Empire East is a unit of Megaworld Properties and Holdings Inc.</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom (632) 841-89-36, fax 817-62-67</p>
